  "body": "fix(launch): guard broker operations with expectedId and expectedGeneration\n\nRefs #1071\n\n## Overview\nAdds incarnation guards to launch tool operations and daemon broker RPC. Operations can require `expectedId` and `expectedGeneration` tuples to guarantee they target the exact process incarnation intended, preventing stale commands from affecting replaced or recycled daemons.\n\n## Changes\n- Wire protocol: `DaemonWireRequest` supports `guarded` wrapper opcode carrying `expectedId`, `expectedGeneration`, and payload request.\n- Daemon broker: validates guard tuple against daemon `id` and `generation`. Rejects mismatched incarnations with `DaemonError.STALE_INCARNATION` and code `ERR_DAEMON_STALE_INCARNATION`.\n- Tool interface: `launch` tool accepts `expectedId` and `expectedGeneration`.\n- Broker capabilities: reports `guardedIdentity: 1` in `DaemonCapabilities`.\n- Completions persistence: enforces schema version 3 (`COMPLETION_SCHEMA_VERSION = 3`).\n- Base wire parser fixture: confirms legacy brokers reject guarded requests.\n- Regression tests: comprehensive protocol and control tests verifying guarded execution, stale rejections, escalation, and capability propagation.\n\n## Verification\n- Local WSL sandbox focused test:\n  `bun test packages/coding-agent/test/launch/guarded-protocol.test.ts packages/coding-agent/test/launch/guarded-control-never-follows-a-replacement.test.ts`\n  Result: 29 pass, 0 fail (107 expectations, 2 files).\n- Scoped TypeScript contract check (tsgo):\n  `tsgo -p tsconfig.scoped.json --noEmit` via temporary package script `bun run --cwd packages/coding-agent check`\n  Result: 0 diagnostics across changed launch production and test files.\n  Note: Whole-package `tsgo -p tsconfig.json --noEmit` emits 5 diagnostics in unrelated `packages/coding-agent/test/task/task-spawn-executor-cwd.test.ts` (unclassified; not asserted baseline).\n",
